 "slug": "5-preflight-check_1110689",
 "title": "5. Preflight check",
 "manual": "Prusa CORE One+ to (Gen 2) upgrade",
 "manual_slug": "prusa-core-one-to-gen-2-upgrade_2435",
 "difficulty": "Easy",
 "updated": "2026-08-14 09:14:37",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": 1136389,
   "title": "Print Sheet",
   "updated": "2026-07-23 13:14:09",
   "lines": [
    {
     "html": "Reinstall the print sheet.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "<strong>Make sure there is nothing on the heatbed</strong>. The heatbed must be clean. Any dirt can damage the surface of both the heatbed and the print sheet.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": "caution",
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "<strong>Attach the sheet by first aligning the rear cutout with the locking pins on the back of the heated bed. </strong>Hold the sheet by the front two corners and slowly lay it down onto the heated bed - <strong>watch your fingers!</strong>",
     "color": "orange",
     "icon": null,
     "level": 0
    },
    {
     "html": "Keep the <a href=\"http://help.prusa3d.com/article/flexible-steel-sheets-guidepost_2195\">print sheet</a> clean for optimum performance.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    },
    {
     "html": "#1 cause of prints detaching from the print surface is a greasy print sheet. <a href=\"http://help.prusa3d.com/article/first-layer-issues_1804\">Use IPA (Isopropyl alcohol) to degrease it</a> if you have touched its surface before.",
     "color": null,
     "icon": null,
     "level": 1
    }
   ],
   "gallery": [
    {
     "original": "https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/24b02b4c2c65e355294f2cff3c4ae7ba_painted.jpeg",
     "large": "https://help.prusa3d.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/24b02b4c2c65e355294f2cff3c4ae7ba_painted-800x600.jpeg",
